    "final_answer": "Final Answer:\n- Report: outputs/reports/hippocampus_sleep_deprivation_report.md\n- Key Results:\n  - The unsupervised analysis grouped the 8 hippocampal RNA‑seq samples into two clusters:\n    - cluster1: sample1, sample2, sample5, sample6\n    - cluster2: sample3, sample4, sample7, sample8\n  - Cluster1 shows coordinated upregulation of immediate‑early / activity‑dependent genes (Fos, Fosb, Arc, Egr1, Npas4, Nr4a1–3, Jun, Junb, Dusp5/6, etc.) and enrichment for synaptic plasticity, neurite remodeling, and stress/hormone‑responsive pathways, consistent with a wake‑activated, sleep‑deprived hippocampus.\n  - Cluster2 is enriched for ribosomal, translational, and mitochondrial energy‑metabolism pathways, with comparatively lower activation of canonical sleep‑deprivation markers, consistent with baseline/control.\n  - Therefore, the samples inferred to be from sleep‑deprived mice are:\n    - **sample1, sample2, sample5, sample6**\n- Artifacts:\n  - Final condition assignments: outputs/tables/sample_condition_assignments.tsv\n  - Differential expression results: outputs/tables/de_results_all_contrasts.tsv\n  - GO enrichment results: outputs/tables/go_enrichment_by_group.tsv\n  - Sleep‑deprivation marker expression: outputs/tables/sleep_deprivation_marker_expression.tsv\n- Figures:\n  - PCA of samples:  \n    ![Sample PCA](outputs/figures/sample_pca.png)\n  - Sleep‑deprivation marker panel heatmap:  \n    ![Sleep-deprivation marker heatmap](outputs/figures/sleep_deprivation_marker_heatmap.png)\n- Caveats & Warnings:\n  - Only 4 samples per group; no genes passed FDR<0.05, so pathway and marker interpretations use relaxed, exploratory thresholds and should be treated as hypothesis‑generating rather than definitive.\n  - Labels are inferred purely from expression patterns and known sleep‑deprivation biology, without external behavioral/physiological validation.\n- Next Steps:\n  - If available, cross‑check these inferred labels against experimental metadata.\n  - Replicate the analysis in independent hippocampal sleep‑deprivation datasets or with count‑based DE methods (e.g., DESeq2/edgeR) using the raw counts.",
